      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Amlodipine 50 mg once daily is a dose that could cause severe harm. It's in the range where overdose causes refractory hypotension and shock, and it can also cause non-cardiogenic pulmonary edema. Amlodipine's half-life is 30 to 50 hours, so the effects would build up and last. You also haven't given a clinical rationale, and none of the patient details you gave would support it.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter 10 mg by mouth once daily.** This is the maximum labeled dose. I can add a note to titrate or reassess blood pressure.\n- **Enter 5 mg by mouth once daily.** This is the standard starting dose.\n- **Help you get more blood pressure control another way.** If 10 mg isn't enough, adding a second agent is safer than going above the maximum. Examples are an ACE inhibitor or ARB, or a thiazide-type diuretic.\n\nIf you think there's a real reason for a dose this far outside the labeled range, please discuss it with a pharmacist or your attending first. That decision should go through those channels, not through me. Tell me which dose you'd like and I'll enter it."
      }
